  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant force\nthis weekend with triple digit heat during the afternoon hours\ntoday and Sunday. Low temperatures tonight will struggle to get\ndown to the mid 60s to mid 70s, making for uncomfortable sleeping\nconditions for those without air conditioning. The Extreme Heat \nWarning continues through 10pm Sunday. \n\nThere will be enough instability with a shortwave trough\napproaching from the southwest this afternoon and evening to\ninitiate a few dry thunderstorms. HREF max ensemble wind gust\nguidance continues to support the potential for damaging wind\ngusts as a primary threat, further noting the inverted-v forecast\nsoundings across the area. A Red Flag Warning for fire zones 134,\n135, 136, and 137 continues for this afternoon due to the\nlightning risk on dry fuels. As an aside, haze and some smoke will\ncontinue at times to be a problem from upstream wildfires.\n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing through\nat least the early and middle part of next week, with highs in the\n90s to around 100 degrees each day.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThe only deviation was to expand the slight chance PoPs this\nevening and overnight. \n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in the heat products through\ntomorrow evening, and for thunderstorms to occur, especially in\nthe southwest tonight. There is low confidence on the exact\nlocations that a severe wind gust may occur though.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in smoke and haze reducing\nvisibility between 1 mile and 6 miles through tomorrow evening.\nThere is similar confidence in the Red Flag Warning for later\ntoday.",
